+neither. Rewrite rather than append — neither is a log — but never drop what is
+finished. Work that closes is marked closed and keeps its entry, what remains is
+hoisted above it, and a short summary sits at the top so a reader can stop early
+without paying for the whole file. A status file that deletes its own history
+saves a few tokens and gives up the one cheap check on what actually happened;
+the summary is what keeps that affordable, not amnesia. A handover that instructs
+its own deletion is the same failure with a deadline — whatever quietly moved
+into it dies on schedule.
